---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: "Visa Info"
description: "F-1-D Digital Nomad Visa income thresholds, family multipliers, and other requirements."
---
<div class="content-page">
<header class="region-header">
  <h1>F-1-D Digital Nomad Visa — Income Requirements</h1>
  <p class="region-header__intro">
    General guidance on the income thresholds and other requirements for Korea's Digital Nomad
    (Workation) visa. This page is informational only — see the disclaimer at the bottom before
    relying on it.
  </p>
</header>

<section class="region-section">
  <h2>Minimum annual income by age and region</h2>
  <p>
    Thresholds are set as a multiple of Korea's Gross National Income (GNI) per capita
    ({{ visaRules.gniReferenceYear }} reference year: ₩{{ visaRules.gniPerCapitaKrw | krw }}).
    Non-capital areas — including population-decrease-designated counties that sit inside
    capital-tier provinces — get a lower multiplier than the capital area.
  </p>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="visa-threshold-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Age</th>
          <th scope="col">Capital area</th>
          <th scope="col">Non-capital area</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for band in visaRules.ageBands %}
        <tr>
          <td>
            {% if band.maxAge %}{{ band.minAge }}–{{ band.maxAge }}{% else %}{{ band.minAge }}+{% endif %}
          </td>
          <td>₩{{ (visaRules.gniPerCapitaKrw * band.multiplierCapitalArea) | round | krw }}
            <span class="mock-note">(×{{ band.multiplierCapitalArea }})</span></td>
          <td>₩{{ (visaRules.gniPerCapitaKrw * band.multiplierNonCapitalArea) | round | krw }}
            <span class="mock-note">(×{{ band.multiplierNonCapitalArea }})</span></td>
        </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="data-provenance">
    Source: Ministry of Justice (법무부) F-1-D announcement, {{ visaRules.version }}
    (effective {{ visaRules.effectiveFrom }}).
  </p>
</section>

<section class="region-section">
  <h2>Bringing family</h2>
  <p>
    Accompanying spouse and minor children raise the required income to a flat family
    multiplier, regardless of the applicant's age:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Capital area — GNI × {{ visaRules.familyMultiplier.capitalArea }} =
      ₩{{ (visaRules.gniPerCapitaKrw * visaRules.familyMultiplier.capitalArea) | round | krw }}</li>
    <li>Non-capital area — GNI × {{ visaRules.familyMultiplier.nonCapitalArea }} =
      ₩{{ (visaRules.gniPerCapitaKrw * visaRules.familyMultiplier.nonCapitalArea) | round | krw }}</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="region-section">
  <h2>Other requirements</h2>
  <dl class="cost-summary">
    <div><dt>Minimum applicant age</dt><dd>{{ visaRules.additionalFacts.minApplicantAge }}
      <span class="mock-note">({{ visaRules.additionalFacts.minApplicantAgeExemption }})</span></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Health insurance</dt><dd>≥ ₩{{ visaRules.additionalFacts.healthInsuranceMinCoverageKrw | krw }} coverage</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Initial stay</dt><dd>{{ visaRules.additionalFacts.initialStayYears }} year</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Max stay</dt><dd>{{ visaRules.additionalFacts.maxStayYears }} years (with renewals, +{{ visaRules.additionalFacts.extensionIncrementYears }}/yr)</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Work restriction</dt><dd>{{ visaRules.additionalFacts.workRestriction }}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Convertible from</dt><dd>{{ visaRules.additionalFacts.convertibleFromVisas | join(", ") }}</dd></div>
  </dl>
  <p>{{ visaRules.additionalFacts.eligibleApplicantSummary }}</p>
</section>

<section class="region-section">
  <p class="empty-state">{{ visaRules.disclaimer }}</p>
</section>
</div>
